## The two numbers

On the demonstration brand, reallocating the same weekly budget of {{ v('budget.total_weekly') }}
by marginal return, under the stated floors, ceilings, change limit and the acquisition cost
allowance, gains {{ v('budget.headline.gain_over_last_year_weekly') }} a week over last year's
mix on the true curves ({{ v('budget.headline.gain_over_last_year_annual') }} a year), and the
calibrated model's plan captured {{ v('budget.headline.share_captured') }} of the truth optimal
gain against {{ v('budget.headline.share_captured_uncalibrated') }} for the uncalibrated model.
That is one seed. Across the {{ v('budget.regret.calibrated.seeds') }} seed regret study the
calibrated plan captured {{ v('budget.regret.calibrated.share_captured') }} of the optimal gain
({{ v('budget.regret.calibrated.share_captured_lower') }} to
{{ v('budget.regret.calibrated.share_captured_upper') }}), a weekly gain of
{{ v('budget.regret.calibrated.gain_weekly') }} ({{ v('budget.regret.calibrated.gain_lower') }} to
{{ v('budget.regret.calibrated.gain_upper') }}), and the uncalibrated plan captured
