## What is here

- **A market with known truth.** {{ v('sim.geos') }} geos over {{ v('sim.weeks') }} weeks,
  seven paid channels with true carryover, saturation and return, spend planned with a stated
  correlation between channels, and display and retargeting spend that follows demand.
  {{ v('sim.customers') }} customers with known treatment effects and the four quadrants;
  {{ v('sim.paths.users') }} user paths with the incremental credit of every touch known.
- **Two mix model backends on one interface.** `own` (geometric adstock, Hill saturation, a
  log linear baseline with additive media, a coarse grid then Nelder-Mead over rolling origins,
  a moving block bootstrap of {{ v('mmm.own.bootstrap_replicates') }} replicates) and `bayes`
  (PyMC-Marketing, the same transforms as priors, {{ v('mmm.bayes.chains') }} chains of
  {{ v('mmm.bayes.draws') }} draws, divergences and R hat recorded). Graded on a recovery
  study of six conditions with {{ v('recovery.own.seeds_per_condition') }} seeds for `own` and
  {{ v('recovery.bayes.seeds_per_condition') }} for `bayes`. Median absolute error on a
  channel's return: `own` {{ v('recovery.own.median_abs_error_overall') }} with
  {{ v('recovery.own.coverage_overall') }} interval coverage, worst in
  {{ v('recovery.own.worst_condition') }} at {{ v('recovery.own.worst_condition_error') }};
  `bayes` {{ v('recovery.bayes.median_abs_error_overall') }} with
  {{ v('recovery.bayes.coverage_overall') }} coverage, worst in
  {{ v('recovery.bayes.worst_condition') }} at {{ v('recovery.bayes.worst_condition_error') }}.
- **A geo lift test with power.** Stratified assignment, pre-registered under plan hash
  `{{ v('geo.plan_hash') }}` before its data existed, the SRM gate {{ v('geo.srm_passed') }},
  difference in differences {{ v('geo.did.estimate') }} ({{ v('geo.did.lower') }} to
  {{ v('geo.did.upper') }}) and synthetic control {{ v('geo.sc.estimate') }} with
  {{ v('geo.sc.placebo_permutations') }} placebo permutations, against a true lift of
  {{ v('geo.truth') }}.
- **The loop.** The posted result becomes a pseudo observation for `own` and a lift test
  measurement for `bayes`. On the tested channel `own` moved from
  {{ v('calibrate.own.roas_before') }} to {{ v('calibrate.own.roas_after') }} against a truth of
  {{ v('calibrate.own.roas_true') }}, and its error on that channel across
  {{ v('calibrate.own.recovery.seeds') }} seeds fell from
  {{ v('calibrate.own.recovery.tested_error_before') }} to
  {{ v('calibrate.own.recovery.tested_error_after') }}. The calibration weight passed its interior
  test ({{ v('calibrate.weight.interior') }}).
- **The real randomized experiment.** Hillstrom's {{ v('data.hillstrom.rows') }} customers: the
  men's email raised conversion by {{ v('email.mens.conversion.effect') }}
  ({{ v('email.mens.conversion.lower') }} to {{ v('email.mens.conversion.upper') }}) and spend by
  {{ v('email.mens.spend.effect') }} per customer, with Benjamini-Hochberg across segments.
- **Uplift evaluated as uplift.** T and X learners with Qini and a policy value curve at a
  stated cost per email. On the real test split the sure things rule earned
  {{ v('targeting.hillstrom.sure_things.policy_value_test') }} per thousand customers and the T
  learner {{ v('targeting.hillstrom.t_learner.policy_value_test') }}, with every Qini interval
  including zero; on the simulator, where the effects are known, the X learner's Qini is
  {{ v('targeting.sim.x_learner.qini') }} against {{ v('targeting.sim.everyone.qini') }} for everyone.
- **Lifetime value with a holdout.** BG/NBD and Gamma-Gamma fit by maximum likelihood on
  {{ v('clv.customers') }} customers of Online Retail II and checked on the next year: the model
  over predicts holdout purchases by {{ v('clv.holdout.purchases_predicted_over_actual') }} overall
  (the fitted dropout probability after a purchase is {{ v('clv.bgnbd.dropout_after_purchase') }})
  and by {{ v('clv.holdout.top_decile_purchases_predicted_over_actual') }} in the top decile; the
  PyMC-Marketing cross check agrees to {{ v('clv.crosscheck.max_relative_difference') }}. The
  allowance it feeds into the optimizer holds {{ v('budget.allowance_infeasible') }} at its floor,
  because that channel's fitted curve never pays back within it.
- **Attribution beside the truth.** Six rules including exact Shapley over
  {{ v('attribution.shapley.coalitions') }} coalitions. Last touch hands display and retargeting
  {{ v('attribution.over_credit.last_touch_share') }} of conversions against a true incremental
  share of {{ v('attribution.over_credit.true_share') }}; the calibrated mix model says
  {{ v('attribution.over_credit.model_share') }}. Every rule over credits that channel most.
- **A registry on a live API.** Plans stored with the model version, the spec hash, the inputs'
  hash and the expected outcome with its interval; experiments with their plan hash; results
  refused without one; the audit row committed before the response. Writes are token gated,
  because this is a demonstration.

